      "summary": ": Today at Cardrona 19 August 2026 — Cardrona is open for a bluebird day after several days of cold weather and fresh snow, with cool south to west winds despite the sunshine. Grooming teams worked overnight, and 10 terrain areas are open, including Main Basin, Captains, Soho, Little Willows, Big Willows, Mt Cardrona, Arcadia Chutes and Summit. Ski Touring Access is also open. Nine of 10 lifts are running, including McDougall’s Chondola, Whitestar Express, Valley View, Captains Express, T-Bar, Soho Express and Willow’s Quad, with Wells Pipe Platter closed. Six of nine terrain parks are open, while Peoples Pipe, Olympic Pipe and Big Air are closed. Main Basin lifts are scheduled from 8:30am, with Captains, T-Bar, Soho and Willows following from 9am. The access road is chain free, although chains must still be carried because of an active road hazard advisory. Three of six car parks are open, with Carparks A and B full and capacity available at The Yard, Valley View and The Pines.",
