      "summary": ": Today at Treble Cone 19 August 2026 — Treble Cone is open for a clear, sunny day with cool southerly/westerly winds and plenty of good snow. Morning groomer laps are recommended while the snow remains firm, with sunshine expected to soften the snowpack and improve off-trail conditions through the day. Home Basin Express, Saddle Quad and Beginner Platter are open, with Home Basin opening at 8:30am and Saddle Basin at 9am. Home Basin, Saddle Basin, Matukituki Basin, Summit Slopes, Motatapu Chutes, Backcountry Access, Skinning Access and Powder Bowl are open, while Sundance is closed. A Freeride World Tour event is taking place in the upper Saddle from Summit to Crags, with a managed crossing on High Street. The access road is chain free, but all vehicles must carry chains because of an active road hazard advisory. Carpark 2 and Carpark 3 are full, while Carpark 1 has space.",
